{
  "_comment": "Per-user, per-machine Claude Code settings for DPF. COPY this file to `.claude/settings.local.json` (gitignored) and edit. It is NOT loaded as-is; only `settings.local.json` is. It takes precedence over the committed `.claude/settings.json`. Put machine-specific paths, OS-specific hooks, and personal permission grants here -- never in the committed settings.json. Keys beginning with `_` are documentation and are ignored by Claude Code.",

  "_comment_worktree_hook": "Canonical worktree PLACEMENT is handled by worktree-create.mjs in the PLUGIN hooks.json, and must stay ONLY there: WorktreeCreate hooks create the worktree themselves, so defining it in both places creates TWO worktrees (asserted by plugin-hooks-wired.test.mjs). If the plugin hook plane is not loaded, Claude falls back to its nested .claude/worktrees location against AGENTS.md \u00a712 \u2014 the work-shape banner reports that worktree as non-conformant at session start. The hook below is the separate, still-optional MCP-config SYNC. Its original rationale \u2014 that .mcp.json carries a bearer token \u2014 no longer holds: .mcp.json is tracked and references ${DPF_MCP_BEARER_TOKEN} from the environment, carrying no secret.",
  "hooks": {
    "WorktreeCreate": [
      {
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "node \"${CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR}/scripts/hooks/run-hook.mjs\" sync-mcp-worktrees",
            "statusMessage": "Syncing MCP config to new worktree...",
            "async": true
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },

  "_comment_permissions": "Machine-specific allow-entries that should NOT be committed. The examples below are the Windows-host entries that previously lived in the committed settings.json -- keep them only if they match YOUR machine, otherwise replace the paths/values with your own (e.g. Read(/Users/<you>/dpf-backups/**)) or delete the block entirely.",
  "permissions": {
    "allow": [
      "Read(//d/DPF/**)",
      "Read(//d/backups//**)",
      "Bash(MSYS_NO_PATHCONV=1 docker exec dpf-sandbox-1 env)"
    ]
  }
}
